<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Lanfang Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1777 CE – 1884 CE · capital Mandor</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Self-governing Hakka mining polity in West Borneo, sometimes called the first republic in Asia, that lasted over a century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luo-fangbo">Luo Fangbo</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakka-people">Hakka</a> scholar and migrant from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangdong">Guangdong</a>, organised Chinese gold miners near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pontianak-sultanate">Pontianak</a> and in 1777 founded the Lanfang kongsi at Mandor. Allied with the Pontianak Sultanate, it grew into a substantial state controlling mines, farmland and trade routes inland.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Lanfang was headed by an elected leader (the taige) assisted by officials, and decisions involved consultation among its members, which has led some writers to call it a republic, though the label is debated. It levied taxes, administered justice and maintained a militia. Most of its people were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakka-people">Hakka</a> miners and farmers, with temple worship to Chinese deities.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> tolerated Lanfang as a semi-autonomous ally longer than other kongsis. When its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-asheng">Liu Asheng</a> died in 1884 they moved to take control, crushed resistance in 1884 to 1885 and annexed it into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lanfang-republic.jpg" alt="Lanfang Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original bitmap flag by Reddit user u/pcdandy, uploaded to Wikimedia Commons by WordforOrange Vector version by me · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lanfang_Republic_Reconstructed_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1777 CE – 1884 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mandor</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Luo Fangbo, Liu Asheng</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese folk religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hakka Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Indonesia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lanfang Kongsi</dd></dl></aside></div>

